From 035a34fecaf9677d043b7ce811e639ee81a64de1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Priyadharshini Gowthaman <pgowtham@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 22:48:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] UPSTREAM:PROTOCOL: sigma_dut: Fix missing ieee80211w for 6G
 PMF-optional AKMs

The common PMF-handling switch in cmd_ap_config_commit() (ap.c),
reached via the skip_key_mgmt label as well as by falling through
the AKM switch, special-cases AP_WPA2_EAP_SHA256 under
AP_PMF_OPTIONAL to emit ieee80211w=2 on the 6 GHz band, where PMF is
mandatory, and ieee80211w=1 elsewhere. The else branch covering every
other AKM reaching AP_PMF_OPTIONAL unconditionally wrote
ieee80211w=1 regardless of band, which disables PMF on 6 GHz and
violates the 6E mandatory-PMF requirement for those AKMs. Add the
same check_band(dut, BAND_6G, link_id) check already used for
AP_WPA2_EAP_SHA256 so the else branch also emits ieee80211w=2 on
6 GHz.

Patch-dependency: 119-UPSTREAM-PROTOCOL-sigma_dut-CAPI-support-for-EPPKE-SAE-key-mgmt.patch

Signed-off-by: Priyadharshini Gowthaman <pgowtham@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 ap.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ap.c b/ap.c
index c3ba943..3e1338b 100644
--- a/ap.c
+++ b/ap.c
@@ -12217,7 +12217,10 @@ skip_key_mgmt:
 				else
 					fprintf(f, "ieee80211w=1\n");
 			} else {
-				fprintf(f, "ieee80211w=1\n");
+				if (check_band(dut, BAND_6G, link_id))
+					fprintf(f, "ieee80211w=2\n");
+				else
+					fprintf(f, "ieee80211w=1\n");
 			}
 			if (dut->ap_key_mgmt == AP_WPA2_PSK_SAE ||
 			    (akm_values & (AKM_SAE | AKM_WPA_PSK)) ==
-- 
2.34.1
